'' A FOR loop over a UDT counter drives the operator protocol.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/diagnostics/src/for-udt-counter.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' GOLDEN: expected/for-udt-counter.out

'' It DECLINED until the protocol was built, and this file asserted the decline -- one
'' statement not lowered. What it is really guarding against is the thing that came
'' BEFORE the decline: a CONSTANT AGGREGATE for the implicit step, an aggregate ADD and
'' an aggregate compare, all of which passed the verifier and then killed the emitter.
'' The golden now pins the calls instead -- 'operator for' once, then a test-first loop
'' through 'operator next( counter, limit )' with 'operator step' on the back edge.

'' An 'icmp.sle' is NOT an assertion here -- 'operator next' compares two integers in
'' its own body, and asserting its absence would fail for the right code.
